    "result_text": "All 29 tests pass. The change is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## What I implemented\n\nThe rule \"reject creating an owner when the owner's city already contains 50 or more owners (409)\" is now enforced in the `POST /api/owners` OfficeFloor pipeline via four new artifacts plus one wiring change:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (function) \u2014 counts existing owners whose city matches (case-insensitively, consistent with `AssignCustomerCode`) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n2. **`OwnerCityCapacityConflictException`** (checked exception) \u2014 so it surfaces in the `throws` clause and is matchable by an escalation handler.\n3. **`OwnerCityCapacityConflictExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT` with a `ProblemDetail`, mirroring the existing household/telephone conflict handlers.\n4. **Escalation YAML** mapping the exception to its handler.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted a `checkCityCapacity` step after the household-uniqueness check and before `build`, under `govern: [ transaction ]` like its neighbours.\n\nI placed the check before `build`/`save` (reading the request DTO via `@Val`), so the per-city count excludes the not-yet-persisted owner \u2014 meaning exactly the 51st create in a city is the one rejected, matching the existing `Cp18Tests` acceptance test.",
